<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('../partials/head', { title, appName, seo: typeof seo !== 'undefined' ? seo : undefined }) %></head>
<body data-force-theme="dark">
    <main class="landing-shell">
        <nav class="landing-nav">
            <a class="brand" href="/" style="padding:0"><%- include('../partials/brand-logo') %></a>
            <div class="landing-nav-links">
                <a href="/">Home</a>
                <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a>
                <a href="/demo">Demo</a>
                <a href="/faqs">FAQ</a>
                <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
            </div>
            <div class="toolbar-actions landing-nav-actions"><a class="button" href="/sign-in">Sign in</a><a class="button primary" href="/sign-up">Create account</a></div>
            <button class="landing-menu-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" data-landing-menu-toggle>
                <span></span><span></span><span></span>
            </button>
            <div class="landing-mobile-menu" data-landing-menu>
                <a href="/">Home</a>
                <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a>
                <a href="/demo">Demo</a>
                <a href="/faqs">FAQ</a>
                <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
                <div class="landing-mobile-actions">
                    <a class="button" href="/sign-in">Sign in</a>
                    <a class="button primary" href="/sign-up">Create account</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </nav>
        <section class="legal-shell">
            <span class="badge brand">Legal</span>
            <h1><%= legalTitle %></h1>
            <p class="muted">These terms apply to <%= appName %>, a GitHub repository security scanning and workflow platform.</p>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>Contact: <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a></span>
                <span>Website: <a href="<%= websiteUrl %>"><%= websiteUrl %></a></span>
            </div>
        </section>

        <% if (legalSlug === 'terms') { %>
            <section class="legal-content">
                <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
                <p>By creating an account, accessing a workspace, installing the GitHub App, or using <%= appName %>, you agree to these Terms, the Privacy Policy, Refund Policy, and any checkout disclosures shown at purchase.</p>
                <h2>2. Service Description</h2>
                <p><%= appName %> provides GitHub repository security scanning, finding triage, team workflow, notifications, audit activity, and reporting. The service is not a penetration testing firm, legal advisor, or guaranteed vulnerability prevention system.</p>
                <h2>3. Accounts and Access</h2>
                <p>You are responsible for account security, team member access, provider permissions, and all activity under your workspace. Do not share credentials, bypass limits, attack the service, or use <%= appName %> for unlawful activity.</p>
                <h2>4. GitHub App Connections</h2>
                <p>When you install the GitHub App, you authorize <%= appName %> to access selected repository metadata and code content needed to perform scans and generate findings. You can revoke access from GitHub or workspace settings.</p>
                <h2>5. Plans and Billing</h2>
                <p>Pricing, usage limits, included seats, repositories, and billing terms are displayed before purchase. Payment processing will be handled by the selected checkout provider. Access may be paused if a payment fails, is disputed, or the plan is cancelled.</p>
                <h2>6. Security Findings</h2>
                <p>Findings are generated by automated rules and may include false positives or miss issues. You remain responsible for reviewing results, validating risk, and deciding whether code changes are required.</p>
                <h2>7. Intellectual Property</h2>
                <p><%= appName %>, its interface, scanner logic, reports, branding, and platform materials are owned by the operator or licensors. Your code, repositories, and uploaded workspace data remain yours.</p>
                <h2>8. Availability and Changes</h2>
                <p>We may update, improve, suspend, or discontinue parts of the service. We work to keep the platform reliable, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free access.</p>
                <h2>9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
                <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, <%= appName %> is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including lost profits, lost data, security incidents, or business interruption.</p>
                <h2>10. Contact</h2>
                <p>For account, billing, or legal questions, contact <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
            </section>
        <% } else if (legalSlug === 'privacy') { %>
            <section class="legal-content">
                <h2>1. Overview</h2>
                <p>This Privacy Policy explains how <%= appName %> collects, uses, and protects information when you visit the site, create an account, connect GitHub repositories, invite team members, or use scanning and reporting features.</p>
                <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
                <p>We may collect account information, team member emails, GitHub App installation metadata, repository metadata, scan results, findings, audit events, notification preferences, usage logs, device information, and support messages.</p>
                <h2>3. Repository Data</h2>
                <p>Repository access is used to run security checks, create findings, build reports, and support workflow features. We do not sell repository code. GitHub access should be limited to the repositories selected during app installation.</p>
                <h2>4. How We Use Information</h2>
                <p>We use information to operate workspaces, authenticate users, connect providers, run scans, send notifications, improve the product, prevent abuse, provide support, and comply with legal or payment processor obligations.</p>
                <h2>5. Service Providers</h2>
                <p>We may use trusted providers for hosting, email delivery, analytics, logging, security, payment processing, and customer support. These providers process information only as needed to provide their services.</p>
                <h2>6. Cookies and Analytics</h2>
                <p>We may use cookies or similar technologies for login sessions, preferences, product analytics, fraud prevention, and performance measurement. Browser settings may allow you to block or delete cookies.</p>
                <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
                <p>We retain data while your account is active and as needed for security, audit, legal, billing, dispute, and operational purposes. You may request deletion where applicable by contacting support.</p>
                <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
                <p>Depending on your location, you may request access, correction, deletion, portability, restriction, or opt-out of certain processing. We may verify your identity before processing a request.</p>
                <h2>9. Contact</h2>
                <p>For privacy requests, contact <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
            </section>
        <% } else if (legalSlug === 'refund-policy') { %>
            <section class="legal-content">
                <h2>1. Digital Service Refund Policy</h2>
                <p><%= appName %> is a digital SaaS product. Once a workspace is activated and service access is delivered, fees are generally non-refundable unless required by law or approved by support.</p>
                <h2>2. Refund Requests</h2>
                <p>Refund requests are reviewed case by case. To request review, contact <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a> with your account email, workspace name, purchase date, transaction reference if available, and reason for the request.</p>
                <h2>3. Billing Errors</h2>
                <p>If you believe you were charged incorrectly, contact support as soon as possible. Confirmed duplicate charges or billing errors may be corrected to the original payment method.</p>
                <h2>4. Cancellations</h2>
                <p>Cancellation stops future access or renewal according to the selected checkout terms. Cancellation does not automatically refund prior charges.</p>
                <h2>5. Chargebacks</h2>
                <p>Please contact support before opening a payment dispute. Chargebacks may result in workspace suspension while the dispute is reviewed.</p>
            </section>
        <% } else { %>
            <section class="legal-content">
                <h2>Do Not Sell or Share</h2>
                <p><%= appName %> does not sell personal information for money. Some analytics, advertising, attribution, or similar technologies may be considered "sharing" or "targeted advertising" under certain privacy laws.</p>
                <p>You may request to opt out by emailing <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a> with the subject line "Do Not Sell or Share Request." Include the email address associated with your account so we can process the request.</p>
                <p>We may need to verify your identity before completing certain privacy requests.</p>
            </section>
        <% } %>

        <footer class="landing-footer compact-footer">
            <div class="landing-footer-brand">
                <a class="brand" href="/" style="padding:0"><%- include('../partials/brand-logo') %></a>
                <p class="muted small">Repository monitoring, scanner workflow, team accountability, and security reporting for small engineering teams.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="landing-footer-grid">
                <div>
                    <h3>Product</h3>
                    <a href="/demo">Demo</a>
                    <a href="/#pricing">Pricing</a>
                    <a href="/faqs">FAQ</a>
                    <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Legal</h3>
                    <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
                    <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
                    <a href="/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>
                    <a href="/do-not-sell">Do Not Sell/Share</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </footer>
        <%- include('../partials/cookie-consent') %>
    </main>
    <script src="/public/js/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
